1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,507
Your site does work in the background:

2
00:00:03,507 --> 00:00:07,667
it clears caches, publishes scheduled content and removes old data.

3
00:00:07,667 --> 00:00:13,080
The Background Tasks module shows that work, changes when it runs, and runs it on demand.

4
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:14,220
Let's see how.

5
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:21,941
A site does work that no visitor asks for.

6
00:00:21,941 --> 00:00:28,768
It clears caches, publishes content on schedule, removes old data and keeps search indexes current.

7
00:00:28,768 --> 00:00:34,229
Modules register this work as background tasks, and the tasks run even without

8
00:00:34,229 --> 00:00:36,440
the Background Tasks module.

9
00:00:37,190 --> 00:00:41,141
The Background Tasks module adds a page to see and control them.

10
00:00:41,141 --> 00:00:45,092
You see what ran and what runs next, change a schedule, switch a

11
00:00:45,092 --> 00:00:47,180
task off, and run it on demand.

12
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:52,260
Access needs the Manage background tasks permission, held by the Administrator role.

13
00:00:56,454 --> 00:01:00,625
Let's open Tools, Features, and search for Background Tasks.

14
00:01:00,625 --> 00:01:03,280
The module is in the Tasks category.

15
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:04,544
Select Enable.

16
00:01:04,997 --> 00:01:10,443
A message confirms the feature is enabled, and Background Tasks appears in the Tools menu.

17
00:01:10,443 --> 00:01:11,577
Let's open it.

18
00:01:15,814 --> 00:01:20,595
Each background task of the site has a row with its title and description.

19
00:01:20,595 --> 00:01:25,794
Badges show whether the task is enabled, when it last ran, and when it runs next.

20
00:01:26,261 --> 00:01:30,417
The Last run badge shows a check mark when the run succeeded, how

21
00:01:30,417 --> 00:01:33,169
long ago it started and how long it took.

22
00:01:33,169 --> 00:01:35,451
A task that never ran says never.

23
00:01:35,926 --> 00:01:38,919
The List and Grid buttons switch the layout.

24
00:01:38,919 --> 00:01:43,826
The Grid layout shows the last run and the next run in columns of their own.

25
00:01:44,303 --> 00:01:48,099
Search filters the tasks by title or description.

26
00:01:48,099 --> 00:01:54,243
The Status filter offers Enabled, Disabled, Running or queued, and Last run failed.

27
00:01:58,502 --> 00:02:01,811
Select the title of a task to open its details.

28
00:02:01,811 --> 00:02:06,619
The Execution card gives the status, the last run with its duration and

29
00:02:06,619 --> 00:02:10,552
trigger, the next run, and the completed and failed runs.

30
00:02:11,066 --> 00:02:17,076
The Settings card shows the schedule, the enabled state, and whether the task is atomic.

31
00:02:17,076 --> 00:02:23,406
Recent runs lists the most recent runs with their start, duration, trigger, result and error.

32
00:02:27,616 --> 00:02:30,181
To change when a task runs, select Edit.

33
00:02:30,181 --> 00:02:33,749
The Properties tab holds the description and the schedule.

34
00:02:33,749 --> 00:02:35,366
The title is read-only.

35
00:02:35,825 --> 00:02:40,538
The schedule is a cron expression, which follows the time zone of the site.

36
00:02:40,538 --> 00:02:45,715
Text that is not a cron expression, such as every night, is rejected when you save.

37
00:02:46,176 --> 00:02:49,817
Reset Schedule puts the default schedule back in the field.

38
00:02:49,817 --> 00:02:53,179
Let's enter a valid cron expression instead, and save.

39
00:02:53,179 --> 00:02:55,756
A message confirms the task was updated.

40
00:02:56,210 --> 00:03:00,558
The background service applies the saved schedule at its next check, and the

41
00:03:00,558 --> 00:03:02,520
Next run badge then follows it.

42
00:03:02,986 --> 00:03:07,661
Use Tenant Pipeline lets the task generate URLs in the background.

43
00:03:07,661 --> 00:03:12,920
The Advanced tab sets a lock timeout and expiration, in milliseconds, for a

44
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:16,166
distributed lock feature such as Redis Lock.

45
00:03:20,388 --> 00:03:24,582
To run a task right away, open its Actions menu and run it from there.

46
00:03:24,582 --> 00:03:26,900
The task runs whatever its schedule.

47
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:30,488
A message confirms the task is queued and will run shortly.

48
00:03:30,944 --> 00:03:34,293
The row follows the run without reloading the page.

49
00:03:34,293 --> 00:03:38,524
Usually within a few seconds, the Last run badge shows the result.

50
00:03:38,988 --> 00:03:42,583
A disabled task can be run on demand too, which lets you check

51
00:03:42,583 --> 00:03:44,168
it before you enable it.

52
00:03:44,168 --> 00:03:46,018
Its schedule is not affected.

53
00:03:46,470 --> 00:03:49,461
To run several tasks together, select them.

54
00:03:49,461 --> 00:03:53,856
The Actions menu of the list then offers Enable, Disable and a run

55
00:03:53,856 --> 00:03:55,810
action, after you confirm.

56
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:04,609
Disable stops a task from running on its schedule, once the background service

57
00:04:04,609 --> 00:04:06,035
picks up the change.

58
00:04:06,035 --> 00:04:10,370
The badge changes to Disabled, and the Next run badge says not scheduled.

59
00:04:10,824 --> 00:04:13,634
Enable puts the task back on its schedule.

60
00:04:13,634 --> 00:04:17,204
A disabled task keeps its settings, so nothing is lost.

61
00:04:21,404 --> 00:04:25,487
When a run fails, the Last run badge turns red, a Failed runs

62
00:04:25,487 --> 00:04:30,666
badge counts the failures, and the error message appears under the description.

63
00:04:30,666 --> 00:04:34,504
The details page adds the full error and its stack trace.

64
00:04:35,254 --> 00:04:39,784
Each server keeps the execution state in memory, so a restart clears it.

65
00:04:39,784 --> 00:04:43,617
In a web farm, a server shows only its own runs, which calls

66
00:04:43,617 --> 00:04:48,264
for session affinity, and running a task on demand affects only the server

67
00:04:48,264 --> 00:04:50,064
that handled the request.

68
00:04:52,064 --> 00:04:54,302
That's the Background Tasks module:

69
00:04:54,302 --> 00:04:58,615
see what ran, change a schedule, switch a task off, and run it on demand.

70
00:04:58,615 --> 00:05:00,034
Thanks for watching.

